  thesis:'BRIDGE\'s creative industries thesis rests on infrastructure before financing. Without recording studios, artists cannot access the royalty streams that royalty-backed financing requires. Without authenticated provenance, heritage textiles cannot command the international premiums that make artisan livelihoods viable. BRIDGE builds the infrastructure first — and the financing instruments the infrastructure makes bankable follow as a natural second step.',
  thesis2:'The sector\'s cross-sector multiplier is underappreciated. Ghana\'s creative identity is the brand that makes Tourism compelling, the content that makes diaspora connection meaningful, and the proof-of-concept that makes Technology investment in local markets credible. When a Ghanaian artist captures 40% of streaming revenue instead of 7%, that is not just a better model. That is the economic infrastructure of cultural self-determination.',

